step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple baseline: mean of the full model pool to see performance baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error on the full model pool to see if weighting improves over simple mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the full pool to see if robust central tendency improves over weighted mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the full pool to see if trimming extreme errors improves over the median baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test the best single model hypothesis by evaluating rf alone.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"rf"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the reduced, high‑performance pool1 to see if inverse‑error weighting improves on the best single rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool2 using inverse_error to see if adding FT_rf and CWT_rf improves over pool1 weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a dba combination on the smaller, more correlated pool1 to see if iterative averaging improves over weighted mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a simple mean over the smaller correlated pool1 to see if reducing variance improves over weighted or dba.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the smaller correlated pool1 to see if simple central tendency improves over weighted and mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the smaller correlated pool1 to see if trimming extreme errors improves over median and weighted on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Evaluate a weighted combination over the full model pool to see if inverse‑error weighting can beat the single rf baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the small correlated pool1 using inverse_error to see if it beats the median pool1 result.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the larger correlated pool2 using inverse_error to see if adding FT_rf improves over weighted pool1 and mean pool2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean over pool2 to see if adding FT_rf improves over pool1 mean/median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool2"}

